  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound in question and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 (UGT2B4), as it is identified as a target of multiple entities that are themselves targets of UGT2B4. Specifically, the compound is linked to CWR22R, which in turn is a target of 3Alpha,24,29-Trihydroxyolean-12-En-28-Oic Acid, Androstanedione, and Mycalenitrile 13, all of which are known to interact with UGT2B4. This indicates that the compound may act as a substrate or modulator of UGT2B4, potentially influencing its activity. The consistent presence of these intermediates in the pathway underscores a possible mechanism involving UGT2B4 as a key enzyme in the metabolic processing of these compounds. The evidence suggests that the compound may be a substrate or a regulator of UGT2B4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
